IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fpa-dates`

-- Family Provision Act 1969 (ACT) -- the rules both seats share: the s 9 time limit (a regulative rule) and the s 20
-- bar on taking provision out of property already distributed. Nothing here is exported; the claimant's questions
-- (fpa-claimant.l4) and the beneficiary's questions (fpa-beneficiary.l4) call these rules, so the two seats cannot
-- disagree about them.
--
-- Edition: Family Provision Act 1969, A1969-15, Republication No 12 (R12), effective 12 December 2023, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/A1969-15.txt.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Family Provision Act 1969: the shared rules`

§§ `s 9 -- the time for applying`

-- The party to the regulative rule, and the step.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `file the application`

-- s 9 (1): "an application for an order under section 8 shall be made within a period of 6 months after the date when
-- administration in respect of the estate of the deceased person has been granted."
-- s 9 (5): the application is "deemed to have been made on the day when the notice of motion or other document
-- instituting the application is filed."
-- The days allowed are counted from the grant (day 0) to the last day of the period (or of an extension, s 9 (2), (3)).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 9 -- apply within 6 months after the grant` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `file the application`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the application for provision was not filed within 6 months after the grant of administration (or within the time the Supreme Court extended it to) (s 9)"

-- Runs the rule over one filing on a day (counted from day 0). FULFILLED means in time. Not exported; the DEONTIC is
-- built here, never taken as an input.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filed in time under s 9` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 9 -- apply within 6 months after the grant` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the applicant` `file the application` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4 (2): a grant made outside the ACT and sealed by the Supreme Court is taken to be granted in the ACT "on the date
-- when it was sealed". The person gives that date as the date of the grant.
-- s 9 (1): the last day of the 6 months.
GIVEN `the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the 6 months after` `the grant` MEANS `the grant` `plus months` 6

§§ `s 20 -- property already distributed`

-- s 20 (2): the Supreme Court "shall not direct that provision be made for a person out of any property that has been
-- the subject of a distribution referred to in subsection (1) if --
--   (a) the distribution was properly made for the purpose of providing for the proper maintenance, education or
--       advancement in life of a person who was totally or partially dependent on the deceased person immediately
--       before the death of the deceased person; or
--   (b) the distribution was made -- (i) more than 6 months after the date when administration of the estate was
--       granted; and (ii) before the administrator had notice of the application for the order or, if an application was
--       made under section 9 for an extension of time ..., the application under section 9;
--   and the property that was so distributed has vested in possession of any person."
-- READING (fork F7): the closing words "and the property ... has vested in possession" attach to (b) only, as their
-- placement after (b) (ii) and before nothing else suggests; the other reading attaches them to (a) and (b) both.
-- "Properly made" for a dependant's maintenance is a judgment: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `made for a dependant's maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the grant` IS A DATE,
      `distributed on` IS A DATE,
      `the administrator had notice first` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the property has vested in possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 (2) bars the distributed property` `made for a dependant's maintenance` `the grant` `distributed on` `the administrator had notice first` `the property has vested in possession` IF
        `made for a dependant's maintenance`
    OR  (    `the six months end` `falls before` `distributed on`
         AND (NOT (`the administrator had notice first`))
         AND `the property has vested in possession`)
    WHERE
        `the six months end` MEANS `the last day of the 6 months after` `the grant`
